#: e82b76d221974cc182d0c875095b9d5f
msgid "The SpeedyBeeF405 Mini supports up to 5 PWM outputs. The pads for motor output M1 to M4 on the ESC connector, plus M5(LED) for LED strip or another PWM output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:102
#: a818b856e77b4633b10023b57b1f14ee
msgid "The PWM is in 3 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:104
#: aad5d4b8364449ea81eb51a429d9e2f4
msgid "PWM 1-2 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:105
#: 1c4c162e5c6f436dbd55ac4c35ea26df
msgid "PWM 3-4 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:106
#: b43a5fcd0f034111be4136d70e916d1c
msgid "PWM 5 in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:108
#: 0bd520529a824c1da4e74f8bf52d4ff4
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot. Channels 1-4 support bi-directional DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:112
#: 16a66bd29a6d4c5db0c3e9ca50d0047e
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:114
#: 1162947427864db2aa6a27f882ba4962
msgid "The SBUS pin, is passed by an inverter to RX2 (UART2 RX), which can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except PPM/CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2. CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 require the RX2 and TX2 pin be connected instead of the SBUS pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:116
#: f1b97acc8a054661afa732c736640446
msgid "SRXL2 requires :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS<SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` be set to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:117
#: 81f321a74dc54a25a30aa946c7db6753
msgid "Fport should be connected to TX2 via a bi-directional inverter and :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS<SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` be set to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:119
#: 9ba1ee87eab74bbd86618b32127106b5
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM (SBUS requires external inversion on other UARTs). See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:121
#: 0bc35612a8e2453a9d0187ddcf859d1f
msgid "the \"4V5\" pins are powered when USB is connected. Be careful not to present too much load to the USB source or voltage droop may occur. All other 5V pins are only powered when battery is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:124
#: d1d63346ace942659db4753e0be1dacd
msgid "Bluetooth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:126
#: e27041d538f24364b8e19b3713c91543
msgid "The SpeedyBeeF405-Mini has an integrated wireless module connected to UART4 but its BLE Bluetooth is not compatible with existing ArduPilot ground stations for Windows or Android."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:129
#: 86b3a73b995d49b1b5935d8eafad7382
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405-mini.rst:131
#: 5c5edbea2543465693b6d15a59bbbcd8
msgid "The SpeedyBeeF405-Mini supports using its internal OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver). External OSD support such as DJI or DisplayPort is supported using UART1 or any other free UART. See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2` for more info."
msgstr ""

